var FT={"Flexible Fighting":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Jaeger Fighting Style. Bonus Action off-hand attack with one-handed weapons, no ability modifier on it, and +1 damage on both while wielding two weapons.","full":"**Extra Attack.** When you attack with a weapon you wield in one hand, you can make an extra attack as a Bonus Action with a different weapon you wield in one hand. Do not add your ability modifier to that extra attack's damage unless it is negative. You cannot do this if you used the Nick mastery this turn.\n**Paired Weapons.** While wielding two weapons, you gain a +1 bonus to the damage rolls of both.","pre":"Jaeger level 2 Fighting Style feature"},"Focused Fighting":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Jaeger Fighting Style. Learn one more Adrenaline Art and gain 1 more Adrenaline Point.","full":"You learn one additional Adrenaline Art and gain 1 additional Adrenaline Point.","pre":"Jaeger level 2 Fighting Style feature"},"Curious":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Origin feat. Borrow a skill proficiency until your next Long Rest. Learn a creature's Resistances and Vulnerabilities after Initiative.","full":"**Learn.** When you make an ability check with a skill you lack, you can become proficient in that skill until you finish a Long Rest. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.\n**Observe.** Right after you roll Initiative, pick one creature you can see in the same combat. You learn its Resistances and Vulnerabilities."},"Faithful":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Origin feat. Once per Long Rest turn a failed save against Charmed or Frightened into a success. Rolling a 1 on a D20 Test gives Heroic Inspiration.","full":"**Divine Clarity.** If you fail a saving throw against the Charmed or Frightened condition, you can choose to succeed instead. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.\n**Trial of Faith.** When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, you gain Heroic Inspiration."},"Grizzled":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Origin feat. Proficiency Bonus added to saves against Frightened, half food and water, and Heroic Inspiration when you become Bloodied.","full":"**Overcome.** On a saving throw against the Frightened condition, add your Proficiency Bonus to the roll.\n**Survive.** You need half as much food and water, and you have Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to forage for food and water.\n**Withstand.** When you become Bloodied, you gain Heroic Inspiration.","fx":{"notes":[["Bonus","Saves against the Frightened condition (Grizzled): add your Proficiency Bonus"]]}},"Worthless":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Origin feat for levels below 4. Cut your ability scores to a total of 72 or less, then lower each by 1. Gain score increases at levels 4, 8, 12, 16 and 19, to a maximum of 18.","full":"**Worthless.** When you gain this feat, lower your highest ability score (your choice on a tie) until the total of your six ability scores is 72 or less. Then lower each ability score by 1.\n**From the Ashes.** At character levels 4, 8, 12, 16 and 19, increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or two ability scores of your choice by 1 each. You cannot raise a score above 18 with this benefit.","pre":"Level below 4"},"Brutalizer":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Wield a Two-Handed weapon in one hand if your other hand is empty or holds a one-handed weapon. Reducing a creature to 0 Hit Points gives Advantage on your next attack.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Brutal Weaponry.** You can wield a weapon with the Two-Handed property in one hand, as long as your other hand is empty or holds a one-handed weapon.\n**Killing Streak.** When you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points, your next attack roll before the end of your next turn has Advantage.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 16+","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Cannoneer":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Proficiency with Cannons, Bonus Action reload, double damage to objects and structures, and half weight for Cannons and Cannonballs.","full":"Raise Strength by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Cannon Proficiency.** You gain proficiency with Cannons and can reload one as a Bonus Action instead of an action. You can do this only if you have not moved this turn, and your Speed is 0 until the end of the turn afterward. From level 11 this no longer reduces your Speed, and when you take the Attack action you can replace one attack with reloading the Cannon. At level 20 you ignore the Artillery property of Cannons.\n**Siege.** Your attacks with Cannons deal double damage to objects and structures.\n**Strong Back.** Cannons and Cannonballs weigh half as much for you.","pre":"Level 8+, Str 18+","asi":["STR"]},"Cosmos Touched":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Pick a level 1 Abjuration or Transmutation spell. It and Alter Self are always prepared and each can be cast once per Long Rest free.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Cosmos Magic.** Pick one level 1 spell from the Abjuration or Transmutation school. You always have that spell and Alter Self prepared. You can cast each without a spell slot. After you cast either one this way, finish a Long Rest to cast that spell this way again. You can also cast them with spell slots. The ability you raised is the spell ability for them.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Focused Hunter":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Gain 1 Adrenaline Point and learn Weapon Parry, Dodge Step or a Jaeger Additional Adrenaline Art. Points return on a Short or Long Rest.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Improved Focus.** You gain 1 Adrenaline Point, added to any you already have, and learn one new Adrenaline Art. Pick Weapon Parry, Dodge Step or any of the Jaeger's Additional Adrenaline Arts. You regain all expended Adrenaline Points when you finish a Short or Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Marksman":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"Reload Barrel weapons as a Bonus Action. Enemies within 5 feet and Prone targets within 30 feet no longer give Disadvantage on ranged attacks.","full":"Raise Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Fast Hands.** You can reload weapons with the Barrel property as a Bonus Action even if they lack the Light property. If a weapon has both Barrel and Light, you can ignore its Barrel property.\n**Steady Aim.** A hostile creature within 5 feet does not give you Disadvantage on ranged attack rolls, and neither does a Prone creature within 30 feet.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["DEX"]},"Osteomantic Adept":{"cat":"G","hb":"SGEH24","d":"When you cast an Osteomancy spell of level 1 or higher, you can raise its level by 1 at the cost of Necrotic damage to yourself.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Empowered Osteomancy.** When you cast an Osteomancy spell of level 1 or higher, you can sacrifice life force to cast it at one level higher. Roll a number of d6s equal to half the spell's original level (round up, minimum 1) and take that much Necrotic damage, which nothing can reduce or prevent. The first time you do this after a Long Rest, you take no damage.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]}};
